unk rock in the subsequent years."}, {"sourceSlug": "funk-rock", "sourceName": "Funk Rock", "verb": "DEFINES", "targetSlug": "alternative-rock", "targetName": "Alternative Rock", "context": "Funk rock helped define the sound of alternative rock in the 1990s, influencing bands like the Red Hot Chili Peppers and No Doubt."}], "places": [{"name": "Los Angeles, United States", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "Detroit, United States", "role": "Cultural Center"}, {"name": "New York City, United States", "role": "Major Venue"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: funk rock", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "funk-rock"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q835891", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk_rock"], "tags": ["music genre", "Music & Compositions", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Funk rock significantly shaped the trajectory of popular music by promoting a fusion of styles that influenced numerous subsequent genres, including alternative rock and nu-metal, impacting the music industry from the 1980s onward.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-30T01:06:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30504317321", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Music genre that fuses funk and rock elements Created c. 1970.", "newValue": "Funk rock emerged as a distinctive music genre in the early 1970s, primarily in the United States, characterized by its fusion of funk rhythms and rock instrumentation. This genre played a critical role in the evolution of popular music, contributing to the diversification of musical styles that defined the Contemporary era. Influential bands such as the Red Hot Chili Peppers, Fishbone, and Parliament-Funkadelic were pivotal in shaping the sound and appeal of funk rock, bringing together the rhythmic grooves of funk with the electric energy of rock music. This synthesis not only attracted a diverse audience but also laid the groundwork for future genres such as alternative rock and nu-metal.

The genre gained significant traction between the late 1970s and early 1990s, particularly with the release of albums like 'Mother’s Milk' by the Red Hot Chili Peppers in 1989 and 'Truth and Soul' by Fishbone in 1993. Funk rock's hybrid nature allowed it to thrive in a music scene that was increasingly embracing eclectic influences, resulting in numerous chart-topping hits and a vibrant live performance culture. Notably, funk rock bands often engaged in socially conscious themes, addressing issues such as racial inequality and urban strife, reflecting the cultural and political landscape of their times.

The legacy of funk rock is evident in its persistent influence on various musical styles and artists, with its rhythms and aesthetics continuing to inform genres like hip-hop and pop-rock today. Many contemporary musicians cite funk rock as a foundational influence, demonstrating its enduring impact on the music industry. This genre's ability to bridge cultural divides and foster collaboration among diverse artists underscores its significance in the broader narrative of music history."}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T01:06:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30504317321", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The rise of African American musical traditions, particularly funk, in the 1960s laid the groundwork for the genre's development.", "The emergence of rock music as a dominant force in popular culture during the late 1960s created a fertile environment for genre fusion.", "Cultural movements of the 1970s, including civil rights and counterculture, influenced the thematic content and performance styles of funk rock artists."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T01:06:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30504317321", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": ["Funk rock contributed to the diversification of the rock genre, encouraging the blending of musical styles that continues to this day.", "The genre fostered a platform for socially conscious lyrics, influencing subsequent generations of musicians to address political and cultural issues.", "Funk rock's popularity in the late 20th century paved the way for the success of alternative and fusion genres in the 1990s and beyond."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-07-30T01:06:13Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30504317321", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "funk-rock", "sourceName": "funk rock", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-contem